      "title": "Counter-current washing recovers caustic",
      "description": "Mud moves forward (left → right) while wash water moves backward (right → left). Each stage dilutes the soluble soda and alumina left in the mud, so the liquor strength falls from red (first washer) to blue (last). Recovered liquor returns to the circuit; washed mud goes to residue storage. Typically 4–7 washers are used, with flocculant to speed settling.",
